# =============================================================================
#  BlaxkVERSE — .gitignore
#
#  Principle: commit everything a person needs to rebuild and audit this site,
#  and nothing that a command can regenerate.
#
#  So `site/` IS committed even though it is generated — it is the deployment
#  artifact, and a static host serves those files, not the generator. Same
#  reason `evidence/*.json` is committed: it is the proof, and it is small.
#
#  Not committed: dependencies, caches, secrets, and the screenshot dumps
#  (~18 MB of PNGs that come back by running `npm run audit` / `npm run shots`).
#
#  NOTE ON SCOPE: this file lives at the project root (blaxkverse/). Directories
#  are matched with a leading slash where they exist only at the root, so the
#  rules stay correct if this is ever nested deeper.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit a real key. docs/security-threat-model.md (K2, K4) requires that
# only placeholders are tracked, which is why .env.example is force-included.
# A leaked GEMINI_API_KEY is a spend attack; a leaked GITHUB_TOKEN is an account
# risk. Both are read from host environment variables in the deployed service.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
secrets.json
service-account*.json

# --- Dependencies ------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js
.yarn/
bower_components/

# --- Build and test caches ---------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.nox/
.tox/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.turbo/
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Playwright --------------------------------------------------------------
# The browser itself is downloaded per-machine by
# `npx playwright-core install chromium` — never commit it.
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
**/.playwright-artifacts-*/
ms-playwright/

# --- Generated screenshots (regenerable) -------------------------------------
# These are proof artifacts, not source: ~18 MB of PNGs on the last run.
# The measurement JSON beside them IS committed — it is the actual claim and it
# is a couple of hundred kilobytes.
#   npm run audit  → evidence/site-shots/
#   npm run shots  → evidence/shots/
/evidence/site-shots/
/evidence/shots/

# Deliberately NOT a blanket `*.png` / `*.jpg` ignore. The 13 screenshots the
# site serves live in site/assets/img/ and are content — they must be committed
# for the deployment to work. Ignoring image extensions globally would silently
# swallow any real asset added later, which is a far worse failure than a
# slightly larger repository.

# --- Working area ------------------------------------------------------------
# Only relevant if this .gitignore is ever used at a parent level: the GitHub
# evidence harvest (raw API cache, scraped HTML, throwaway scripts) is an input
# to the build, not part of the deliverable.
/recon/
/uploads/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- OS and editor -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
